es and Algorithms, its educational goals, and target audience including students, interview candidates, and developers seeking to improve their algorithmic thinking skills. Document the project's structure with the Strings directory for string manipulation algorithms and explain how users can navigate and utilize this collection effectively. Include guidance on how this repository fits into broader DSA learning pathways and preparation strategies.","progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"README.md","gmt_create":"2026-10-29T22:41:43.2783775+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-10-29T22:53:09.6508457+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"883c7834-2372-466c-bf67-9bd0dfec740b","repo_id":"64740dc0-6043-442f-b6ba-00667255aa15","name":"Getting Started","description":"getting-started","prompt":"Create a getting started guide for the DSA Preparation repository. Include prerequisites such as basic programming knowledge and understanding of time/space complexity. Provide setup instructions for contributing new algorithms and implementing solutions. Document the coding standards and conventions expected for algorithm implementations. Explain how to navigate the repository structure, particularly the Strings directory, and provide guidance on how to add new algorithm categories and implementations following the established patterns.","order":1,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"README.md","gmt_create":"2026-10-29T22:41:43.2801314+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-10-29T22:53:12.8061268+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"cf60b56a-2697-4488-b948-788f30cda93d","repo_id":"64740dc0-6043-442f-b6ba-00667255aa15","name":"String Algorithms","description":"string-algorithms","prompt":"Develop detailed content for the String Algorithms section. Document the purpose of string manipulation algorithms and their importance in computer science and software development. Explain common string problems including pattern matching, text processing, substring operations, and string transformations. Provide implementation guidelines for string algorithms, including best practices for efficiency and readability. Include examples of typical string manipulation tasks and their computational complexity considerations. Document the organizational structure within the Strings directory and how to contribute new string algorithm implementations.","order":2,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"Strings/index.js,Strings/","gmt_create":"2026-10-29T22:41:43.2808503+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-10-29T22:53:07.8449947+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"}],"wiki_items":[{"catalog_id":"883c7834-2372-466c-bf67-9bd0dfec740b","title":"Getting Started","description":"getting-started","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"64740dc0-6043-442f-b6ba-00667255aa15","reference_count":0,"id":"4ffdb353-790d-4563-8cfb-eb78076d8021","gmt_create":"2026-10-29T22:41:51.1475189+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-10-29T22:53:12.8061268+05:30"},{"catalog_id":"55837ba5-716a-418c-b4f0-d13ca2084f48","title":"Project Overview","description":"project-overview","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"64740dc0-6043-442f-b6ba-00667255aa15","reference_count":0,"id":"1af926de-a6f4-41bc-9bb9-b38ec73d6a33","gmt_create":"2026-10-29T22:41:56.56006+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-10-29T22:53:09.6513813+05:30"},{"catalog_id":"cf60b56a-2697-4488-b948-788f30cda93d","title":"String Algorithms","description":"string-algorithms","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"64740dc0-6043-442f-b6ba-00667255aa15","reference_count":0,"id":"d67fefc0-6fbb-4dfb-a2aa-5ce1818d6d83","gmt_create":"2026-10-29T22:42:06.7470849+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-10-29T22:53:07.8449947+05:30"}],"wiki_overview":{"content":"\u003cblog\u003e\n# DSA Preparation Project Analysis\n\n## 1. Project Introduction\n\n### Purpose Statement\nThe **dsa_prep** project appears to be a Data Structures and Algorithms preparation repository, likely intended for learning, practice, or interview preparation purposes. The minimal structure suggests this is either an initial setup or a placeholder project awaiting implementation.\n\n### Core Goals and Objectives\n- Provide a structured environment for DSA problem-solving practice\n- Serve as a foundation for algorithmic coding exercises\n- Support learning and mastery of fundamental computer science concepts\n\n### Target Audience\n- Computer science students preparing for technical interviews\n- Developers seeking to improve their algorithmic thinking skills\n- Individuals studying data structures and algorithms\n\n## 2. Technical Architecture\n\n### Current Project Structure\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[dsa_prep] --\u003e B[Strings/]\n    A --\u003e C[README.md]\n    B --\u003e D[(Empty Directory)]\n```\n\n### Design Patterns\nGiven the current minimal structure, no specific design patterns are implemented yet. The project follows a simple flat organization with:\n- Root-level documentation (README.md)\n- Category-based directory structure (Strings/)\n- Empty implementation directories ready for code organization\n\n### System Relationships\nThe project currently has no inter-component dependencies as it contains only:\n- Documentation file\n- Empty category directories\n\n## 3. Key Implementation\n\n### Main Entry Points\n- **README.md**: Project documentation and introduction\n\n### Core Modules\nCurrently, no core modules exist. The `Strings/` directory appears to be designated for string-related algorithm implementations but remains empty.\n\n### Configuration Approach\nNo configuration files are present in the current structure.\n\n### External Dependencies\nNo external dependencies are configured at this stage.\n\n### Integration Points\nNo integration points are defined yet.\n\n## 4. Key Features\n\n### Functionality Overview\nThe project is currently in its initial state with:\n- Basic project setup\n- Placeholder directory structure for organizing DSA problems by category\n- Minimal documentation\n\n### Implementation Highlights\n- Clean, minimal starting point for DSA practice\n- Organized directory structure ready for categorization\n- Simple README for project context\n\n## 5. Conclusion and Recommendations\n\n### Project Architecture Summary\nThe dsa_prep project represents a clean-slate approach to building a comprehensive DSA preparation resource. The current architecture is intentionally minimal, providing a foundation that can be expanded based on specific needs and preferences.\n\n### Architectural Strengths\n- **Simplicity**: Easy to understand and navigate\n- **Flexibility**: Open structure allows for various organizational approaches\n- **Scalability**: Ready to accommodate growing content\n\n### Potential Improvement Areas\n- **Content Development**: Primary area needing attention - implementing actual DSA solutions\n- **Documentation**: Expand README with detailed instructions and examples\n- **Structure Definition**: Establish clear naming conventions and folder organization\n- **Testing Framework**: Consider adding test cases for algorithm validation\n\n### Actionable Recommendations\n1. **Define Content Strategy**: Determine which data structures and algorithms to implement\n2. **Establish Organization Pattern**: Choose between language-specific or concept-based organization\n3. **Add Templates**: Create starter templates for common DSA problem types\n4. **Include Examples**: Add sample solutions with explanations\n5. **Set Up Testing**: Implement automated testing for algorithm correctness\n\n### Next Steps for Project Evolution\n1. Populate the Strings directory with string manipulation algorithms\n2. Create additional category directories (Arrays, Trees, Graphs, etc.)\n3. Implement core algorithmic patterns and techniques\n4. Add comprehensive documentation and examples\n5. Consider adding performance analysis and complexity discussions\n\nSources:\n- [README.md](README.md)\n\n\u003c/blog\u003e","gmt_create":"2026-10-29T22:41:24.7920335+05:30",